    "description": "Vintage Dip Pen Nib Collection  Esterbrook, Mallat, Muller & Others in Bering Cigar Box\nAssorted collection of previously owned metal dip pen nibs and illustrated pen-nib boxes, housed in a wooden Bering Claro cigar box.\nThe collection includes assorted loose metal nibs and multiple small cardboard boxes from several manufacturers. Several boxes were reported as unopened.\nPhotographed Manufacturers and Markings:\nEsterbrook & Co.  314 Relief Pens, boxes marked 100 Pens and Made in U.S.A.\nHeintze & Blanckertz  German steel pen nib packaging, including boxes marked 144 Stuck Schreibfedern\nHerm. Muller A.G.  Leipziger Stahlfederfabrik, No. 3703, marked 1 Gross Eilfedern\nJ.B. Mallat  French Plumes Metalliques, No. 12 Pointes Moyennes, boxes marked 100\nBering Claro  wooden cigar box marked Tampa, Florida\nSome Esterbrook packaging includes distributor information referring to Cairo, Egypt.\nThe assortment contains numerous loose metal pen nibs of various shapes and sizes, including some gold-colored pieces.\nCondition:\nPreviously owned collection with age- and storage-related wear.\nThe cardboard boxes show varying amounts of edge wear, discoloration, scuffs, creases, and surface marks. Some labels and packaging remain visually colorful, while others show more substantial wear.\nSeveral boxes were reported as unopened. Their internal contents and quantities have not been independently inspected.\nThe loose metal nibs show varying surface finishes and possible discoloration or oxidation. Individual nibs have not been examined for corrosion, bends, or writing performance.\nThe wooden cigar box shows visible storage and handling wear.\nTesting Classification: Untested. No writing or functional testing was performed.\nThe actual number of pen nibs and the contents of unopened boxes have not been verified. Quantities printed on packaging refer to the manufacturer's labeled contents and do not establish current quantities.\nThe exact production dates and metal compositions are unknown.\nIncluded Contents:\nOne Bering Claro wooden cigar box containing the photographed assortment of pen-nib boxes and loose metal dip pen nibs.\nAdditional Information:\nThese items were donated and previously owned; their complete history is unknown. Photographs show the actual items and are part of the description. Only photographed contents are included unless specifically stated otherwise. Measurements are approximate when provided, and colors may vary due to lighting or display settings. Descriptions may contain unintentional errors. Buyers should review all photographs and ask questions before bidding. The items are sold AS-IS according to the testing and condition stated above.",
